# Getting Started with the Theme Scaffold

Welcome to the {{theme_name}} WordPress block theme scaffold! This guide walks you through cloning, configuring, and launching your new theme.

## 1. Clone or Download

Clone or download the scaffold repository. All `.mustache` files are templates—do not use them as-is.

## 2. Configure Placeholders

Edit your `mapping.json` file with the values for all mustache placeholders. See [Mustache Placeholder Reference](./placeholder-schema-and-usage.md) for the full variable list and sample.

## 3. Run the Templating Script

Run the script (e.g., `node bin/replace-placeholders.js --map mapping.json`) to generate your theme files.

## 4. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
composer install
```

## 5. Build and Test

```bash
npm run build
npm run test
npm run lint
```

## 6. Activate Your Theme

Zip and upload, or symlink to your WordPress install and activate in the dashboard.

See [SCAFFOLD-USAGE.md](./SCAFFOLD-USAGE.md) for more details.

